---
source: crates/togi/tests/cli/main.rs
expression: "help(\"night-guard\")"
---
Return to the day when the night is over, before the tuner starts

Runs first in every tuning boot. When the morning time has passed it restores the day's boot selection exactly and reboots; the tuner never starts. Otherwise it exits 0 and the tuner may start, however many boots the night has had: a failure never ends a night. A tuning boot entered from the boot menu gets a night that ends at the next morning time.

An error exits unsuccessfully, which keeps the tuner from starting unguarded.

Usage: togi night-guard [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state-dir <path>
          State directory
          
          [default: /var/lib/togi]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  sudo togi night-guard   End the night if the morning has come, or let the tuner start
